{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review tattoo licensing and regulation",
        "additional_details": "Require:\r\nUsing an artist licence number to order stock\r\nRegular council checks\r\nSeparate licences ie semi permanent, body & medical.\r\n \r\nWe call for stronger regulation of the tattoo industry to protect clients and legitimate artists.\r\n \r\nLicensing should require proven training and experience, with robust council checks to prevent unlicensed home studios. Clinical waste must be properly disposed of and tattoo ID cards enforced.\r\n \r\nArtist licence numbers should be required to purchase professional stock, with separate licences for tattooing, semi-permanent makeup, body piercing and medical tattooing.",
        "background": "Identify measures to:\r\nStop inexperienced tattoo artist gaining licensing\r\nPrevent unlicensed home studios\r\nEnsure proper disposal of clinical waste (tattoo ID cards).",
